    "name": "Star Chart",
    "description": "A planetarium night: a deep blue-black dome of sky with a visible gradient, a Milky-Way band and thousands of seeded stars (size and colour variety, gentle deterministic twinkle) over a low dark horizon of hills, trees and an observatory; antique celestial-atlas graphics drawn over it in fine gold line — coordinate grid, ticked ecliptic, constellation stick figures, engraved figure outlines, small serif star names. The invented sky turns about a pole so stars rise, drift and trail; chosen stars brighten one by one, gold lines draw between them into original constellations (each a concept, each star a part), an engraved figure fades up, a name plate writes on, a presenter's arrow sweeps to what is being named, and a dashed line connects two constellations.",
